Integration & policy decisions:
- The port *rejects* unsupported IPA (raises) rather than approximating. Real
  Wikipedia {{IPAc-en}} output frequently contains symbols outside this English
  inventory (ʔ, tap ɾ, χ for non-English names; some rhotic/disambiguation
  forms). So the caller needs a fallback policy: try the canonical port first;
  on failure fall back to the existing diaphonemes.ipa_to_respell() best-effort,
  and keep respell_derived=true plus a provenance note (e.g. respell_method
  'canonical' vs 'heuristic'). Smoke-test over a sample of real extracted IPA to
  measure the failure rate before committing to any policy.
